    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABHe5W2Q",
      "title": "sep/112-113: OP Sepolia OPE batcher and proposer rotation",
      "author": "donoso-eth",
      "number": 1571,
      "body": "Adds `src/tasks/sep/112-op-sepolia-set-batcher` and `src/tasks/sep/113-op-sepolia-proposer-rotation`, the OP Sepolia OP Enterprise key rotation for the Oct 15 ceremony ([solutions#1546](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/solutions/issues/1546)):\r\n\r\n- **sep/112** sets the batcher `0x64EDa4F93314ECd619bd4f79D8d1F8112A4E6e16` on the `SystemConfigProxy` `0x034edD2A225f7f429A63E0f1D2084B9E0A93b538` with `setBatcherHash`, executed by the FoundationUpgradeSafe. The unsafe block signer is pinned to its current value, so only `setBatcherHash` is emitted — one call, not two.\r\n- **sep/113** rotates the `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` (5) proposer to `0x9884C33C65111DA7Bbed0e63cD2392F503b135F5` with `SetDisputeGameArgs`, signed by the L1PAO. Impl, anchorStateRegistry and the zero bond are read live and kept.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n**Pending:** `SystemConfig.owner()` is still the EOA `0xfd1D2e72…` and must `transferOwnership` to the FoundationUpgradeSafe before sep/112 executes; config.toml overrides slot `0x33` until then.\r\n\r\nTasks carried over from #1568, which keeps sep/114 (unsafe signer, Oct 30). Nonce pins follow sep/110-111: sep/112 FUS 79, sep/113 L1PAO 58 / FUS 80 / SC 72.\r\n\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-09T06:53:33Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-13T10:49:29Z",
      "additions": 405,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABISBbhw",
      "title": "eth/074-075: FUS and FOS signer rotation",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1577,
      "body": "Swap owner 0x7F1D4FE689B73B628285454667B93cfd09409f27 for 0xa564C83958f7F9fA5a255a540EF5e49445873104 on the Foundation Upgrade Safe (nonce 73) and Foundation Operations Safe (nonce 122) via GnosisSafeRotateSigner. Threshold 5 and owner count 7 unchanged.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-13T23:22:18Z",
